GCC's -Wreturn-type does not consider a switch over every enumerator to be
exhaustive, so `context::fpa_rounding_mode()` trips -Werror=return-type.
Turn the last case into `default:` so the switch is exhaustive for GCC too
without introducing unreachable code (which clang's warning set dislikes).

Reported upstream as <https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/issues/10584>.

diff --git a/src/api/c++/z3++.h b/src/api/c++/z3++.h
--- a/src/api/c++/z3++.h
+++ b/src/api/c++/z3++.h
@@ -4152,7 +4152,7 @@
         case RNE: return expr(*this, Z3_mk_fpa_rne(m_ctx));
         case RTP: return expr(*this, Z3_mk_fpa_rtp(m_ctx));
         case RTN: return expr(*this, Z3_mk_fpa_rtn(m_ctx));
-        case RTZ: return expr(*this, Z3_mk_fpa_rtz(m_ctx));
+        default:  return expr(*this, Z3_mk_fpa_rtz(m_ctx));
         }
     }
 
